# Committed on purpose, and load-bearing.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are INLINED BY NEXT.JS AT BUILD TIME — they are not
# read from the environment at runtime. Putting them only in wrangler.jsonc
# `vars` (which are runtime Worker env) is therefore not enough for anything the
# browser executes: `next build` sees them unset and compiles the fallback in
# `src/lib/api/browser.ts` down to the literal string "http://localhost:8080".
#
# That is not hypothetical. It shipped on RsvpVault on 2026-07-27: server-
# rendered pages worked fine (they read INTERNAL_API_URL at runtime, where
# wrangler vars do exist), so the marketing page and the smoke test both passed,
# while every browser-side call — login included — quietly tried to reach
# localhost and failed with a bare network error.
#
# These values are public by definition: they end up in a JavaScript bundle any
# visitor can read. Nothing secret belongs in this file. Real secrets stay
# Worker secrets (`wrangler secret put`) and are only ever read server-side.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.advault.3pandalabs.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://advault.3pandalabs.com
